  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.0\n- Migrate One Call API from 2.5 (retired by OpenWeatherMap) to 3.0; requires a \"One Call by Call\" subscription\n- Breaking: GetWeatherOneCallAsync now calls One Call API 3.0 and is no longer obsolete\n- Breaking: Replace GetWeatherOneCallHistoricAsync with GetWeatherOneCallTimeMachineAsync (returns OneCallTimeMachineInfo)\n- Add GetWeatherOneCallDaySummaryAsync and GetWeatherOneCallOverviewAsync\n- Add OneCallOptions.IncludeAlerts, DailyWeatherForecast.Summary and HourlyWeatherForecast.Rain/Snow\n- Add Geocoding API: GetLocationsByNameAsync, GetLocationByZipCodeAsync, GetLocationsByCoordinatesAsync\n- Add GetAirPollutionForecastAsync and GetAirPollutionHistoryAsync\n- Breaking: UnitSystem.Standard returns temperatures in Kelvin (was Celsius)\n- Breaking: IOpenWeatherMapService has new members\n- GetCurrentWeatherAsync validates latitude and longitude\n\n2.2\n- Maintenance updates\n- Replace Newtonsoft.Json with System.Text.Json\n- Change WeatherInfo.CityId from string to int\n- Mark GetWeatherOneCallAsync and GetWeatherOneCallHistoricAsync as obsolete (One Call API 2.5 was retired by OpenWeatherMap)\n\n2.1\n- Extended the 16-day forecast model (DailyWeatherForecastItem) with missing properties\n\n2.0\n- Use unit types from dependency UnitsNet\n\n1.2\n- Major refactoring in wind direction data model\n- Add multilingual support\n\n1.0\n- Initial release",
